index 0000000..7831231
--- /dev/null
+++ b/CANVAS-BUILD-STATE-MAP.md
@@ -0,0 +1,186 @@
+# Canvas Build-State Integration Map (#3591724)
+
+Verified against this working tree (`drupal/canvas` dev-1.x + MR 1214 POC patch) on
+2026-07-10, including a live 7-hop build on `https://c2026.ddev.site`. Corrects the
+assumptions in spec §3 of `2026-07-06_canvas-build-state-TECH-SPEC.md`.
+
+Paths: `<ai>` = `modules/canvas_ai`, `<ui>` = `ui`.
+
+## Turn / loop model (spec §3 correction: there is no polling service)
+
+- The front end drives the loop. DeepChat's `connect.handler` → `runHops()`
+  (`<ui>/src/components/aiExtension/AiWizard.tsx:890-964`) re-POSTs
+  `/admin/api/canvas/ai` with a stable `request_id` while the response says
+  `should_continue: true`.
+- Server: `<ai>/src/Controller/CanvasBuilder.php::render()` sets
+  `$agent->setLooped(FALSE)` (L261) → **one LLM tool-decision per HTTP request
+  ("hop")**. `should_continue = !$agent->isFinished()` (L280). "Finished" =
+  the model returns a turn with no tool call
+  (`ai_agents/src/PluginBase/AiAgentEntityWrapper.php::determineSolvability()`).
+- Agent state is serialized per `request_id` into `CanvasAiTempStore`
+  (PrivateTempStore, `thread_` prefix): restored at `CanvasBuilder.php:200-205`,
+  persisted at :280-288. Deleted on finish/error — **not on abort**, so
+  re-POSTing the same `request_id` resumes the turn (no "continue" message
+  needed; when resuming, incoming messages are ignored in favor of
+  `$agent->fromArray($thread_state)`).
+- Tools selected on hop N **execute at the top of hop N+1**
+  (`AiAgentEntityWrapper.php:497-524`); their structured output is merged into
+  hop N+1's JSON.
+- Active agent: single flat `canvas_page_builder_agent`
+  (`<ai>/config/install/ai_agents.ai_agent.canvas_page_builder_agent.yml`,
+  system prompt inline; `max_loops: 40`). It does not delegate. The old
+  orchestrator + sub-agents exist as config but are dormant. The
+  component-editor agent (`canvas_component_agent`) is separate and only active
+  when set as `main_agent` / in code-editor context.
+
+## Hop response shape (from `CanvasBuilder::render()` JOB_SOLVABLE branch)
+
+```jsonc
+{
+  "status": true,
+  "operations": [ ... ],        // merged tool output; PLAIN ARRAY of {operation:'ADD', components:[...]} in the raw hop JSON
+  "component_updates": { ... }, // (edit_components), canvas_page_data, etc.
+  "should_continue": true,      // false on final hop
+  "message": "...",             // final hop only
+  "progress": [ {               // cumulative narration, every hop
+    "id": "canvas_page_builder_agent", "type": "agent", "name": "...",
+    "description": "Thinking", "status": "running|completed",
+    "generated_text": "...", "agent_runner_id": "<uuid>" } ]
+}
+```
+
+- `progress` is built by `getProgressItems()` (`CanvasBuilder.php:391-453`) from
+  the `ai_agents` status poller; Canvas subscribes only to `Started` +
+  `TextGenerated` (`CanvasBuilder.php:229-232`).
+- Tool results reach the UI as top-level keys consumed by `messageHandlers[]`
+  (`AiWizard.tsx:114-325`): `operations` (ADD-only placements, applied one at a
+  time ~1s apart via `drupalSettings.canvas.layoutUtils.addNewComponentToLayout`),
+  `component_updates`, `canvas_page_data`, code-component keys.
+
+## Live probe results (Risk 1 — validated 2026-07-10)
+
+Adding `AiAgentStatusItemTypes::ToolSelected` to `setDetailedProgressTracking()`
+and echoing the poller's ToolSelected items into the hop JSON worked end-to-end
+on a real build ("hero + one feature section", 7 hops):
+
+| Hop | tools_selected (cumulative)                    | response keys        |
+|-----|------------------------------------------------|----------------------|
+| 1   | — (clarifying-questions turn, `sc:false`)      | status, message, progress |
+| 2   | get_component_details                          | status, sc, progress |
+| 3-4 | + ai_search_rag_search ×2                      | status, sc, progress |
+| 5   | + place_components (selected)                  | status, sc, progress |
+| 6   | + place_components ×2                          | + **operations**     |
+| 7   | (final, `sc:false`)                            | + operations, message|
+
+Facts this establishes:
+
+1. `ToolSelected` items reach the poller in the same hop the LLM selects the
+   tool — one hop **before** the tool's output. A front-end lock gate sees the
+   structural signal early.
+2. Match tools on **`tool_name`** (the function name, e.g. `place_components`,
+   `get_component_details`, `ai_search_rag_search`). The item's `tool_id` is the
+   LLM call id (`toolu_…`), not the plugin id.
+3. `isAgentDecision()` is TRUE for model-chosen tools; poller storage is
+   cumulative per `request_id` and non-draining (`getLatestStatusUpdates()` is a
+   pure load).
+4. Real builds can open with research calls (`get_component_details`,
+   `ai_search_rag_search`) before any `place_components` — a lock gate based
+   only on "first tool is structural" would briefly unlock mid-build. This
+   justifies the `lock_viewport` marker tool (spec Phase 3 hybrid design).
+
+## Viewport (the central canvas area)
+
+- `Viewport.tsx` (`<ui>/src/features/layout/preview/Viewport.tsx`):
+  `.previewContainer` (L94) wraps two double-buffered `<iframe srcdoc>`
+  (`IframeSwapper.tsx`) + a Radix `<Progress>`.
+- Iframes are `pointer-events: none` except in INTERACTIVE mode. **All editing
+  interaction happens outside the iframe**:
+  - portalled overlay layer `features/layout/previewOverlay/`
+    (`ViewportOverlay` → `RegionOverlay` → `ComponentOverlay`) in unscaled
+    coordinates inside `div#canvasPreviewOverlay`;
+  - dnd-kit `<DndContext>` at `app/App.tsx:90`;
+  - hotkeys in `features/editorFrame/EditorFrame.tsx` (Delete → `deleteNode`
+    L132, mod+c/v, `v` interactive toggle; `react-hotkeys-hook` supports
+    `enabled:`).
+  Locking the viewport = neutralize those three + a blocking overlay for
+  INTERACTIVE mode. Overlay precedents: `components/SavingOverlay.tsx`; unused
+  `.loadingOverlay` in `Preview.module.css:35`.
+- Reusable for per-component work: `components/spotlight/Spotlight.tsx`
+  (9-cell scrim with cutout, `blocking` prop; used by `RegionSpotlight` inside
+  `.previewContainer`), `useDataToHtmlMapValue().componentsMap[uuid].elements` +
+  `useSyncPreviewElementSize` for component rects.
+
+## Chat (AiWizard)
+
+- `<ui>/src/components/aiExtension/AiWizard.tsx` renders `deep-chat-react`;
+  input, message list, and the submit↔stop button live in DeepChat's shadow
+  DOM, configured via props. A stop-button style exists
+  (`DEEP_CHAT_SUBMIT_BUTTON_STYLES.stop` ~L530) but the per-turn
+  `AbortController` (~L846) is only aborted on unmount — explicit stop wiring
+  is net-new. Chat history persists in IndexedDB (`aiWizardDB`).
+- Mounted in `AiPanel` (`app/App.tsx:96`) and `PrimaryPanel.tsx:117`.
+- There is **no global Redux "AI turn in progress" flag** — all lifecycle
+  transitions live inside `connectHandler`. (The build-state slice added by
+  this work is the first.)
+
+## Undo / revert
+
+- `redux-undo` wraps `layoutModel` + `pageData` (`<ui>/src/app/store.ts`);
+  middleware `undoRedoActionIdMiddleware` (store.ts:174-229) pushes **one undo
+  entry per dispatched action**; no groupBy → an AI build = N undo steps.
+- `setLayoutModel` (`layoutModelSlice.ts:509`) restores a full snapshot in one
+  action → one undo entry. AI component edits also land in `layoutModel`
+  (`services/preview.ts:176`), so a pre-turn `layoutModel.present` snapshot
+  covers placements and edits.
+- The back end never mutates the page; server autosave
+  (`canvas/api/v0/layout/...`, `AutoSaveManager`) is a single overwritten
+  draft. Turn revert must be client-side.
+
+## Tools (FunctionCall plugins, `<ai>/src/Plugin/AiFunctionCall/`)
+
+| function_name        | plugin id                     | notes                        |
+|----------------------|-------------------------------|------------------------------|
+| place_components     | canvas_ai:place_components    | ADD only; structured output  |
+| edit_components      | canvas_ai:edit_components     | prop edits by uuid           |
+| set_page_value       | canvas_ai:set_page_value      | title/description            |
+| get_component_context / get_component_details / get_current_layout | info tools |
+| ai_agent_verify_task_completion | ai_agent:verify_task_completion | no-op marker precedent (dormant) |
+
+- **No delete-component tool exists**; the FE `operationsHandler` supports only
+  `ADD`.
+- Tools whose output must reach the UI implement
+  `BuilderResponseFunctionCallInterface` + `setStructuredOutput()`
+  (`PlaceComponents.php:126`); the controller merges them into the hop JSON
+  (`CanvasBuilder.php:303-315`).
+- Scaffolding reference: `web/modules/contrib/ai/docs/developers/function_call.md`.
+- Build-mode prompt text lives in `<ai>/src/CanvasAiExecutionStrategy.php`
+  (INCREMENTAL/BATCH, substituted via the `[canvas_ai:execution_strategy]`
+  token) — prompt changes are PHP edits, not config migrations.
+
+## Feature flags
+
+- Template: `disable_real_time_page_generation` in `canvas_ai.settings`
+  (config/install + schema + `<ai>/src/Form/CanvasAiSettingsForm.php`,
+  consumed in `CanvasBuilder.php` ~L259).
+- UI plumbing: `CanvasAiHooks::jsSettingsAlter()` (`<ai>/src/Hook/CanvasAiHooks.php`)
+  → `drupalSettings.canvas.*` → `getCanvasSettings()`
+  (`<ui>/src/utils/drupal-globals.ts`).
+
+## Testing & build
+
+- Playwright: `tests/src/Playwright/` (model: `tests/isolatedPerTest/ai.spec.ts`
+  + `objects/Ai.ts`). Runs isolated throwaway Drupal sites; AI responses are
+  fixture-mocked by `canvas_ai_test`
+  (`<ai>/tests/modules/canvas_ai_test/src/EventSubscriber/CanvasAiRequestInterceptor.php`,
+  slugified prompt → `fixtures/<slug>.json`). Multi-hop sequences need a
+  hop-counter extension (planned in Phase 1).
+- Vitest: `<ui>/tests/vitest/unit/*.test.js` (see `undo-redo-timeline.test.js`).
+- PHP kernel tests per tool: `<ai>/tests/src/Kernel/Plugin/AiFunctionCall/`.
+- Build: `npm run build` in `<ui>` — Drupal loads the **committed**
+  `ui/dist/assets/index.js|css` via the `canvas-ui` library; rebuild before any
+  browser verification. Live dev: `npm run drupaldev` + enable `canvas_vite`.
+- Conventions (AGENTS.md): `npm run fix|lint`, `composer run fix|lint`; narrow
+  tests only, never full suites.
+- Environment: DDEV project `c2026` → `https://c2026.ddev.site`; login via
+  `ddev drush uli`. **Do not re-run `ddev demo-setup`** — it reinstalls the
+  module (destroys local work, including this git repo).
