diff --git a/modules/canvas_ai/src/CanvasAiExecutionStrategy.php b/modules/canvas_ai/src/CanvasAiExecutionStrategy.php
index afcb526..642d3cd 100644
--- a/modules/canvas_ai/src/CanvasAiExecutionStrategy.php
+++ b/modules/canvas_ai/src/CanvasAiExecutionStrategy.php
@@ -32,6 +32,8 @@ final class CanvasAiExecutionStrategy {
 
     In this mode you apply ONE visible change per tool call so the page updates live, section by section, in front of the user.
 
+    - **Lock signal (hard rule):** The moment you begin executing a request that will add or build page sections, your VERY FIRST tool-calling turn — even if that turn is only research (`get_component_details`, searches) — must include a `lock_viewport` call bundled alongside that turn's other call(s). Never spend a separate turn on it, and never delay it until placement. Do not call it for questions, advice, or small single edits (titles, descriptions, prop tweaks).
+    - **Build plan (hard rule):** In that same FIRST tool-calling turn of an approved build, also include one `set_build_plan` call listing every planned section in order (`component_id`, `title`, `size`). Set `size: tall` for content-heavy blocks (heroes, feature grids, stats, FAQs, testimonials, galleries) and `size: short` for slim bands (banners, CTAs, disclaimers, logo strips). Bundle it with the other calls — never as its own turn. Skip it entirely for questions, advice, or small single edits.
     - **One row per call:** Place one top-level row (with its children nested in slots) per `place_components` call. Never combine several top-level rows into a single call in this mode.
     - **A placement result means CONTINUE, not stop (hard rule):** After each `place_components` call the updated layout — including the real UUID of what you just placed — is returned to you. That result is NOT a checkpoint to summarize and yield at. The instant it arrives and the page is not yet complete (K < N below), your very next output — in THIS response, right now, not a later turn — is the next `place_components` call. Row 1 targets the `content` region with placement `inside`. Rows 2+ take the UUID of the row you just placed as `reference_uuid` with placement `below`.
